        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0283" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.932/584: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-22T15:00:00+08:00">February 22, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 22—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>295. Major General Harada called on me this afternoon and made formal expression
                    of regret as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I express our sincere regret for the violation of American Embassy
                            property in Nanking. In this connection I should like to assure you that
                            the Japanese authorities have taken appropriate steps to prevent
                            recurrence of such incidents. As for the question of desecration of
                            American flags we are conducting investigations. It is however most
                            regrettable if such a thing did happen. I therefore express regret for
                            the matter as well.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo, Hankow and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
